    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d987">

                <pb facs="0766" n="690" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg690"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.48/3140</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Parker,
                        representing American interests, to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-16T18:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 16, 1916, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>314. Department’s 330, May 13, 2 p.m. Since Department’s authorization of March
                    20, transportation has been furnished to twenty persons, about half men. There
                    are about 275 on the destitute list of whom probably 100 are native born
                    Americans, the remainder being Mexican women legally married to Americans with
                    their minor children. This latter class would be better off here in any event.
                    Persons other than destitutes who have left have done so principally as the
                    result of urgent telegrams from relatives in the United States. American colony
                    here is practically reduced to those whose business interests require their
                    presence here together with <pb facs="0767" n="691" xml:id="pg691"/> their
                    families and is conservatively estimated at 1,200. Department’s advice relative
                    to departure of Americans is being discreetly made known.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Parker</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
